  "data": {
    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Scintillating Legion",
    "summary": "As the battle begins, you have 3 Flux tokens; a dice is a handy way to track your count.\n\nWhenever one of your **LEGIONES DAEMONICA TZEENTCH** models or units makes a [Hit](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls), [Wound](vsdata:core-rule/wound-rolls), [Advance](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) or Damage roll, a [saving throw](vsdata:core-rule/save-rolls) or a [Hazardous](vsdata:weapon-ability/hazardous) test, you can spend a Flux token after it to re-roll it. Some Stratagems also get extra effects if you spend Flux tokens on them. Each Flux token you spend goes to your opponent.\n\nWhile your opponent has any Flux tokens, whenever one of their models or units makes a Hit, Wound or Advance roll or a saving throw, they can spend a Flux token after it to re-roll it, and that token comes to you. Ignore this paragraph if your opponent's army uses Fates in Flux too.\n\nDuring [your Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase), you get a Flux token if your opponent holds any.\n\n**Designer’s Note**: with fast dice rolling, after you roll several rolls or saving throws together, you can spend any number of your Flux tokens and re-roll as many of those dice as the tokens you spent.",
